    "lawCode": "Amd §696, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6465\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the tax law, in relation to not\nextending collection period after assessment as a result of\nhospitalization for members of the armed forces, astronauts and\nvictims of certain terrorist attacks\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would conform the Tax Law to recently enacted Internal\nRevenue Code provisions.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one of this bill amends section 696 of the Tax Law by adding a\nnew subsection (i) to provide that the continuous hospitalization plus\none hundred eighty days thereafter provisions of subsection (a) do not\napply to the collection of personal income tax liability.\n\nSection two of this bill provides that this act shall take effect\nimmediately and shall apply to taxes assessed before, on, or after the\ndate of the enactment of this act for which there is an outstanding\ntax liability.\n\n CURRENT LAW :\n\nWhen a member of the armed forces or a person serving in support of\nthe armed forces in a combat zone is injured and hospitalized, the\nlimitations period for collections is tolled for the hospitalization\nperiod plus one hundred eighty days thereafter.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nOn December 18, 2015, the President signed H.R. 2029, which became\nPublic Law 114-113. Included in Division Q of this law, which is\nentitled Protecting Americans from Tax Hikes Act of 2015, is the\nWounded Warrior Tax Equity Act. Previously, the Internal Revenue\nService had an extended period of time to collect tax arrears from\nmembers of the armed forces who were hospitalized as the result of a\ncombat injury. This extended period of time equaled the period of\nhospitalization plus 180 days thereafter. The Wounded Warrior Tax\nEquity Act changed this rule by eliminating this extended period of\ntime.\n\nIn this State, we conform to the Internal Revenue Code. However,\nconformity in this instance requires a statutory change. Because this\namendment to the Tax Law levels the playing field for our wounded\nwarriors and no longer places them at a disadvantage, it needs to be\nenacted this year so that the disparate treatment of our wounded\nwarriors can end.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
